# Worktree & Deploy Queue Constitution

## Single Docker host

This machine runs **one** Docker acceptance stack (`8080` / `4173`).

- All deploys use `.\scripts\docker-deploy-queue.ps1` (mutex around `docker-deploy.ps1`).
- Do **not** create a second compose project, `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`, or port offsets for
  “parallel acceptance”.
- If the lock is held: wait or report `DEPLOY_QUEUED` / timeout — never bypass.

Skill: `.cursor/skills/docker-deploy-queue/SKILL.md`.

## Worktree isolation

- Parallel agents or build-contending slices: decide via `worktree-router` before writes.
- Naming: directory `../DGE-<slice-id>`, branch `feat/<slice-id>`.
- Shared OK: Git objects, `~/.m2`, pnpm store. Not shared: working tree, `target/`, `dist/`.
- After an isolated slice is green: `integration-merger` merges (or opens PR) then
  **removes** the worktree (`git worktree remove` + `prune`).

Skill: `.cursor/skills/worktree-isolation/SKILL.md`.

## Pipeline hooks

`delivery-orchestrator` includes placement (start) and integration-merger (before doc sync)
when the slice used an isolated worktree. See `delivery-orchestration-constitution.mdc`.

## Forbidden

- Two sessions writing the same worktree path for different slices.
- Parallel `docker-deploy` from two worktrees.
- Leaving feature worktrees after successful merge without cleanup (unless user opts out).
